
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "events";
    Layout = "~/Views/Shared/_Layout.cshtml";
}

<div class="website-main-content">
    <section class="page-banner-breadcrumbs">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="breadcrumbs">
                <span class="page-name">AllenKids Swaroopnagar</span><span class="seprator">></span><span class="page-name">Events</span>
                <h3 class="title-of-page">
                    Events
                </h3>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="page-section why-choose-allen-kids Event">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-12">
                    <p class="discription">
                        At Allen Kids we focus on co-scholastic activities for the all-round development of Allenites. We put equal emphasis on knowledge, life skills and values. Allen Kids goes beyond academics to ensure that we provide students sufficient opportunities for
                        achieving success.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            MELANGE
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            The pandemic could not snatch away the stage from our talented little Allenites. Allen Fiesta –
                            2020-21 presented “Melange”- The ensemble of fairy tale characters.
                        </p>
                        <p class="discription">
                            The students of Nursery
                            and Prep dressed up as fairy tale characters and enacted so joyfully and passionately that it
                            made way directly into the hearts of the viewers.

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event1.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event2.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            CHRISTMAS CELEBRATION
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            The month of December ended on a jubilant note with Christmas celebration. Christmas
                            Carnival was organised for our little Allenites with offline PTM where parents discussed the
                            progress of their wards and children enjoyed games and dance with Santa .Virtual games and
                            Christmas cards were also made by children in their online session.
                        </p>

                    </div>
                </div>


            </div>

            <div class="row">

                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            STORY TELLING AND SHOW AND TELL COMPETITION
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            As a learning tool, story telling can encourage students to explore their unique expressiveness and can heighten a student’s ability to communicate thoughts and feelings in an articulate, lucid manner. It helps improve their language skills, instills a love of reading and stirs their imagination.
                            Brightening the day with wonderful stories, the Hindi story telling and the English story telling competition were conducted for the children of Nursery and Prep. The vibrant story tellers came forth with interesting tales that reinforced moral values.
                            The show and tell competition was conducted for class Nursery. Children excitedly shared their descriptive narration and communicated their feelings, thoughts and emotions with words on their objects. It helped tiny tots to build their social, emotional ad language skills.
                        </p>


                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event3.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event4.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            (GREY CAPS FOR PG-I AND PG-II)
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            “January opens the box of the year and brings days that are cold and grey”.
                            Physical PTM for classes Playgroup I & II was organized. In the PTM  to engage and recapitulate the learnings of three terms, an inter – class quiz competition was conducted for class PG I and PG II in a very interactive way. All teams participated with great enthusiasm in various rounds comprising of oral questions, riddles, hand – on activities. The children and the parents were awarded with gifts and crowns.
                        </p>

                    </div>
                </div>


            </div>

            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            FUNATHON
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            Your speed doesn't matter, Forward is Forward.
                            Funathon, a day filled with gratification had the same sight. Games play a major role in maintaining a healthy mind, body and soul of the child. As it gives a lot of exercise in forming an overall healthy physique.
                            It is because of the games that children at the very young age interact and engage in the world around them.

                        </p>
                        <p class="discription">
                            The school organised fun filled games for both parents and children like cuddle race, sac race, hurdle race, lemon race, balloon race etc.
                            Colouring competition was also organised for kids where they presented their colourful imagination and creativity.
                            Children and parents showed their talent with the full zeal and enthusiasm.

                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event5.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event6.png" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            GREY CAPS
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            "If you are a true warrior, competition doesn't scare you. It makes you better".
                            Quiz Competition  'GREY CAPS' was organised for Nursery and Prep students. Children's intelligence and power of retention was demonstrated. A platform was provided to them to face challenges and competition. Their excitement and enthusiasm was a visual treat.
                        </p>

                    </div>
                </div>


            </div>
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="play-group-icon-title">

                        <h3 class="page-title">
                            GRADUATION CEREMONY
                        </h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="discription-section">
                        <p class="discription">
                            The month of March came to a close with the graduation ceremony. A wonderful adieu was bid to our children of class prep at DPS Kalyanpur.
                            Students of class Nursery extended a hearty welcome to the seniors. Colourful dance performances were presented and melodious songs were sung by the students.
                            This was followed by the graduation ceremony and the prize distribution ceremony.
                            The school wore a festive look illuminating with shining faces of the Prep students who walked the ramp adorned in traditional convocation gowns and caps.
                            Their  smiling faces were welcomed by rapturous applause from the audience as they received merit certificates on the stage.
                            It was indeed heartwarming to see teary-eyed parents as they watched their angels grow into butterflies ready to fly.

                        </p>


                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-sm-6">
                    <div class="photo-section">
                        <img src="../../content/images/event/event7.jpg" alt="display-photo">
                    </div>
